        "Notes": "Maylender identifies this academy with one erroneously located in Mantua in the 1557 edition of Antonio Francesco Doni`s Libraria (p. 277). Doni might have made an error based on the fact that it was in Mantua where the Argonauti of Casale Monferrato had their Dialogi Maritimi printed in 1547. There is one book associated with this academy that is not in the British Library collections: Gioan Iacopo Bottazzo, Argonavis in laude Argonautarum Academiae Casalensis Pterois equus Caroli quinti imperatori sive Hippographia, Franciscum Moschenium, Pavia, 1553.",
